          "source_text_sha256": "c3f08c20b2b7964e7b98a778dd3f23b2db9d11336af77f4d47ee8b7ef803e09d",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On October 5, 2012, at 11:26 PM, a witness observed for one minute in the sky the silent movement of a bright, orange, oval-shaped object with wings on each side. No other testimonies were collected. Based on the information gathered during the investigation, including:\n\n- No exact information on the azimuth of appearance and disappearance.\n- No information on the angular heights of appearance and disappearance.\n- Lack of angular measurements.\n- No further details on altitude, distance, and size estimates of the object.\n\nWe can conclude that the lack of precision does not allow us to favor any particular hypothesis. This case is classified as \"C,\" an observation of an unidentified phenomenon at this stage, as the lack of elements does not allow for a solid opinion. This testimony is of low consistency: it is vague and detailed, and it lacks fundamental and necessary data for further study. There is only one eyewitness account, with no photo or video documentation. The observation is not particularly strange as it could be a completely mundane object (e.g., a nocturnal bird illuminated by urban lighting, a military plane with lights off, etc.), thus the GEIPAN did not see the need for a field investigation to enrich the file.",
